  - "TIMEZONE": check all rows are in CDT/CST  
  - "OBJECTID": = 10000697078 (ERCOT hub HB_NORTH) – node filter  
  - "ISO": must equal 'E' or 'ERCOT' depending on data  
  - "DALMP": Day‑Ahead price ( $/MWh )  
  - "RTLMP": Real‑Time price ( $/MWh )  
  - Optional: "RTFINAL" flag to keep only final data  

• TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE  
  - "DATETIME": forecast target hour  
  - "PUBLISHDATE": when forecast was issued (helps choose latest if needed)  
  - "OBJECTID": = 10000712973 (ERCOT North load zone)  
  - "DATATYPEID":  
        19060 -> Load forecast  
        9285  -> Wind generation forecast  
        662   -> Solar generation forecast  
  - "VALUE": MW of the forecast  

• TS_LOAD_SAMPLE (actual load)  
  - "DATETIME": hour‑ending timestamp  
  - "OBJECTID": = 10000712973  
  - "DATATYPEID": 9641 (ERCOT actual zonal load)  
  - "VALUE": MW (rename as "RTLOAD")  

• TS_GEN_SAMPLE (actual gen)  
  - "DATETIME": timestamp (5‑min granularity; will later need hourly aggregation)  
  - "OBJECTID": (wind / solar geographic regions)  
        10004189445 → GR_PANHANDLE (wind)  
        10004189450 → GR_WEST      (wind)  
        … (for the summary you may need to sum all GR_ zones).  
    For illustration we will stick to OBJECTID 10004189442 (GR_ERCOT) which is system‑wide.  
  - "DATATYPEID":  
        16  -> Actual Wind generation  
        650 -> Actual Solar generation  
  - "VALUE": MW  

• ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE  
  - "DATETIME": hour stamp (local)  
  - "ONPEAK", "OFFPEAK", "WEPEAK", "WDPEAK": binary peak classifications  
  - "MARKETDAY": groups hours to the same calendar day  
  - "ISO": 'ERCOT' – filter  

MAIN DATE FILTERS / CONDITIONS YOU’LL USE
    WHERE "DATETIME" >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
      AND "DATETIME"  < '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
    AND "OBJECTID" = 10000697078   -- for prices  
    AND "OBJECTID" = 10000712973   -- for load zone elements  
    AND "ISO" ILIKE 'ERCOT%'       -- robustness  

